==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mystic Yulala''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Spiritual Yulala''' when obtained from [[Infernal Tower]] [[Infernal Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Masked Yulala is an overall terrible unit. His stats are very low. On paper, he seems to be a decent addition as a [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attacker]], especially for {{4c}}, however, his really low stats with lack of backswing, somewhat okay range and fast speed turn him into a rather suicidal unit. His damage is also unreliably mediocre, making him not worth using most of the time.

Yulala can be used as a LD attacker on {{4c}}, but there's a catch: there are already more reliable [[:Category:Special Cats|Special]] and [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]] LD units like [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]. Even considering him as a rusher, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie Cat]] exist.

Tragically, he can't even do his job well as a sniper (although that's not his best use), as by the way you obtained him, [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]] and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] outperform him in terms of sniping. To make the matter worse, [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]]'s Surge Attacks are much more reliable at sniping even before [[True Form]] despite his significantly lower DPS; this is due to Uril having more range at a lower speed and cost.

==='''True Form'''===
Spiritual Yulala gains more health, a faster cooldown and now comes with [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic]] abilities. Although his health remains mediocre and [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic enemies]] tend to be aggressive with their high stats, Yulala does have a niche against them. His massive damage ability makes his hits far more punishing against them, and when properly stalled, can quickly melt large amounts of their health.

Yulala is also a viable counter against [[M. Ost]]; something that can't be stalled with your traditional meatshields unless using Talented [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]], as Yulala's heavily good effective DPS can chip M. Ost to death, and M.Ost's Slow/Knockback abilities can mitigate Yulala's suicidal tendencies. Against other Relic enemies, he is only useful against shorter-ranged ones, like [[Relic Bun-Bun]], [[Relic Doge]] and [[Idi:Ne]], as his range prevents him from reaching that far. He can be treated as a safer [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]], but less hard-hitting, however, he can do something that Idi can't: juggle [[Sir Rel]]s. His effective damage; especially when leveled up, is enough to juggle some weaker Sir Rels.

Yulala still has a catch: his anti-Relic niche can be outdone by [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] in most situations, as their disposability and an additional [[Weaken|Weaken]] from their Talents do a lot better at accumulating DPS. But their damage per hit is not enough to counter M. Ost, leaving Yulala still viable against it.

Overall, Yulala is a bit better in this True Form, but it still doesn't fix his issues, as his general usage is still terrible.

