==Trivia==
*His design may be a reference to the character [[wikia:snk:Mudman|Mudman]] from the ''[[wikia:snk:World Heroes (series)|World Heroes]]'' series.
*Masked Yulala's description references the meme [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/cool-story-bro Cool Story, Bro].
*He is [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]]'s son. [[Mystic Mask Yulala]]'s Japanese description calls him the head of his clan, and [[Master Uril (Enemy)|enemy Master Uril]]'s Japanese description says he passed down that same title to his son when he retired.
*It is heavily implied that [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] is the daughter of Masked Yulala, as they both wear masks, have the same white hair and seem to use the same attack. Masked Yulala also mentions "his 12-year old daughter" in his Evolved Form's description, while Spiritual Yulala's Japanese description mentions an "adolescent daughter" as well as Yulala's futile attempts to get her attention. Ururun Cat's description says that her father is a school teacher and Mystic Mask Yulala's description states that he teaches modern dance to kindergartners, further hinting that he is Ururun's father. Their Normal Forms' descriptions also state that both Yulala and Ururun will "join those who have defeated them", suggesting a that they all follow the family tradition of joining those who have defeated them. In [[Sacrifice Apprenticeship]], they even appear together.
*Ururun Wolf's, Masked Yulala's, Master Uril's and [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Fenrir]]'s Japanese descriptions all start with a quote followed by how they joined the Cat Army, which always includes the word 勝手 (''katte'', meaning "selfish", "self-serving" or "acting on one's own without asking").
*Like [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]], the staff held by Yulala resembles his floor within the Heavenly Tower ([[Heavenly Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]]).
*Masked Yulala, [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] and [[Hanasaka Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Hanasaka Cat]] all have similar movement animations.

